WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:06.080
This walkthrough shows how regulations
are maintained in the updated

2
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:12.000
application. In the previous TPMS,
regulation data was kept on five separate

3
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:13.010
maintenance screens.

4
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:17.730
Subpart held the topics of the book,
each with a code and a description.

5
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.220
Subsection held the
sections inside each topic,

6
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.510
and named the Subpart it belonged to.

7
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.470
Regulation was one long list.

8
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.730
For every rule we typed the
section, amendment and title,

9
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:34.930
the Subpart and Subsection
codes, the FAA source link,

10
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:39.600
the sort order, the requirement text,
the means of compliance and the section

11
00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:44.810
root. Regulation Group and Regulation
Group Section were two more screens,

12
00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.950
linking a kind of modification
to the rules it affects.

13
00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.950
In the updated application, this area
is called the Regulatory Library.

14
00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:56.710
Its Regulations tab is
the same complete list,

15
00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.110
made easier to read.

16
00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.690
Each row shows the
section, amendment, title,

17
00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:05.770
subpart, subsection,
section root, source link,

18
00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.550
and whether the rule is active.

19
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.650
Search finds a rule by its
section, amendment or title,

20
00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.890
and Filters narrow the list further.

21
00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:19.020
Opening a rule displays its saved requirement
text and means of compliance in a

22
00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:23.030
readable side panel, together with the
other amendments of the same section,

23
00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.022
and its FAA source is one click away.

24
00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.670
Previous and Next move through the list.

25
00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:32.430
Add Regulation asks for the
same details as before,

26
00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:37.580
grouped into Rule, Text and Placement,
with the subpart and subsection chosen at

27
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.410
the top. Edit uses the same form.

28
00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:45.090
A regulation that a basis or plan
already uses cannot be deleted;

29
00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.330
it can be made inactive instead.

30
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:52.310
Subparts and subsections now live
together under Certification Topics.

31
00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:55.300
The topics of the book
are listed on the left,

32
00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.050
each with its number of subsections.

33
00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:02.160
Selecting a topic shows its subsections,
and how many regulations each one

34
00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:05.910
holds. Add Subpart takes
the code, description,

35
00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:11.130
sort order and active state, and Add
Subsection takes the code and title.

36
00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.890
Opening a subsection
lists its regulations,

37
00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:16.230
so the library reads like a book:

38
00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.560
topic, subsection, rule.

39
00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:23.880
From here, a regulation can be added,
viewed or edited without leaving the

40
00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:28.090
topic. Regulation Groups brings
the two group screens together.

41
00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:32.110
Groups, such as a galley
modification, are listed on the left,

42
00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:35.270
and the selected group shows
the rules it usually affects.

43
00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:38.330
Rules are attached from inside the group.

44
00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.770
The result is one library for every rule:

45
00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:46.040
find it in the list, read it in
place, organise it by topic,

46
00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:48.450
and group it by the kind of modification.
